// Two rooms directly in the world. Anything written at the top of a file
// is read from inside the world, so these are named by their names alone.
object shop_floor: Room in tree
object kiln: Room in tree

// A key in each of two chests, and one in the room beside them: a name
// belongs to what holds it, so none of them is in another's way.
object red_chest: Chest in shop_floor
object blue_chest: Chest in shop_floor
object key: Thing in shop_floor
object key: Thing in shop_floor.red_chest
object key: Thing in shop_floor.blue_chest

// Deeper than what the world holds, a container is named by its path.
object shelf: Chest in kiln
object pot: Chest in kiln.shelf
object lid: Thing in kiln.shelf.pot

// Written before what holds it: where a thing sits does not depend on
// the order it was written in.
object glaze: Thing in kiln.shelf.jar
object jar: Chest in kiln.shelf
